Author: Wallace Chan <naahtec@hotmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jun 15 08:37:53 2026 -0400

    fix(#12442): re-emit assigned-to for stuck handoff work (EAD)
    
    The External Activity Detector (#12342) emitted the assigned-to nudge
    exactly once per transition, gated by `updatedAt > _last_check_epoch`.
    For terminal HANDOFF statuses (pending-test → verifier, pending-ship →
    dm) that single nudge is the ONLY delivery path to an often-event-mode
    agent. If it was missed — dm busy mid-cycle, a cursor gap,
    ack-without-action, or the item was already at the status when the
    detector (re)started so its updatedAt is in the past and the time filter
    hides it forever — the item starved (observed: #12418 sat pending-ship
    48 min until PM hand-injected a wake event).
    
    Fix: for the two handoff statuses only, re-emit the assigned-to nudge on
    a bounded cadence (_HANDOFF_REEMIT_SECONDS = 600s), bypassing the
    updatedAt time filter, until the status changes (which removes the item
    from the open+pending query and ends the re-emit). Idempotent — an
    assigned-to is a wake nudge; a redundant one just makes the agent
    re-check its queue. Worker statuses (approved/open) keep the single-emit
    + time-filter behavior (their worker is presumed already looping).
    
    - harness.py: _HANDOFF_REEMIT_SECONDS, _handoff_emit_at, _handoff_due/
      _mark_handoff_emit, re-emit branch in _check_for_changes.
    - test_harness.py: TestEADHandoffReemit12442 (7 tests); retargeted the
      #12342 time-filter test to a worker status (handoff is now exempt).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

